From d3a47363e82e43cbb466716a3bffbafd6d08d985 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Thomas Bourgoin <thomas.bourgoin@foss.st.com>
Date: Fri, 17 Jul 2026 09:42:42 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 851/913] core: pta: return when we fail to register receive
 channel

The IPCC mailbox test registered the receive channel via
mbox_dt_register_chan() but only logged an error message when the
registration failed (e.g. channel already registered by another
user), then kept running the test as if it had succeeded.

Return the error code immediately when the receive channel
registration fails, so the test is not executed with an unregistered
channel.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [ST downstream https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/optee_os.git 765c6392fe22f79c3b81dff6a5480de353d485b6 core: pta: return when we fail to register receive channel]
Change-Id: Ia2084a83fe06b6b2b872f44e35f05f108f8e1a54
Signed-off-by: Thomas Bourgoin <thomas.bourgoin@foss.st.com>
Reviewed-on: https://gerrit.st.com/c/mpu/oe/optee/optee_os/+/588993
ACI: CIBUILD <MDG-smet-aci-builds@list.st.com>
Domain-Review: Arnaud POULIQUEN <arnaud.pouliquen@st.com>
ACI: CITOOLS <MDG-smet-aci-reviews@list.st.com>
---
 core/pta/tests/mbox.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/core/pta/tests/mbox.c b/core/pta/tests/mbox.c
index 53a5aee57..bf5cb3f2c 100644
--- a/core/pta/tests/mbox.c
+++ b/core/pta/tests/mbox.c
@@ -528,8 +528,10 @@ static TEE_Result ipcc_mailbox_test(void)
 		return TEE_SUCCESS;
 	res = mbox_dt_register_chan(receive_callback, NULL, NULL, fdt, node,
 				    &handle_receive_send);
-	if (res != TEE_SUCCESS)
+	if (res != TEE_SUCCESS) {
 		EMSG("chan handle_receive_send %x", res);
+		return res;
+	}
 
 	notif_register_driver(&mbox_notif);
 
